      ],
      "margin_number": 10,
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "τί βουλόμενος As before, ‘wanting what, do you ... ?’\nἀπολεῖς με ... ‘you will destroy me’, ‘you will be the death of me’. The future of ἀπόλλυμι.",
      "lang": "mixed",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "vocab_entry",
      "order": 6,
      "bbox": [
        605,
        155,
        649,
        862
      ],
      "margin_number": 11,
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "βοῇ χρῶμαι χράομαι (‘I use’) takes the dative (GE p. 180, #190 (e)). The meaning is the same as if βοῶ had been written.",
      "lang": "mixed",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "vocab_entry",
      "order": 7,
      "bbox": [
        645,
        155,
        659,
        729
      ],
      "margin_number": 17,
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "ἐμπεσεῖται Future of ἐμπίπτω – πίπτω πεσοῦμαι ἔπεσον.",
      "lang": "mixed",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "vocab_entry",
      "order": 8,
      "bbox": [
        664,
        156,
        678,
        856
      ],
      "margin_number": 18,
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "τυγχάνεις εἰδώς εἰδώς -ότος is the participle of οἶδα; the infinitive is εἰδέναι.",
      "lang": "mixed",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "vocab_entry",
      "order": 9,
      "bbox": [
        683,
        155,
        715,
        885
      ],
      "margin_number": 20,
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "οὑτοίῚ οὗτος αὕτη τοῦτο + ι is even more demonstrative. ‘These spectators here’. (Note that the neuter is τουτί ταυτί.)",
      "lang": "mixed",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "vocab_entry",
      "order": 10,
      "bbox": [
        724,
        122,
        800,
        893
      ],
      "margin_number": 21,
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "κἀπειπε.... τοῖς θεαταῖς, πολλοῖς δὴ οὖσιν ‘Tell the spectators, being many indeed’. What part of the verb is οὖσιν? Can you recognise it? It is the dative plural of the participle ὤν οὖσα ὄν.",
      "lang": "mixed",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
